# Cover letters

Write one Markdown letter for one company and one role. Use facts from the base resume in `Base/` and from the job description only. Do not invent employment, metrics, or personal history.

If `Base/` has no resume, stop and ask for one.

## Shape

Use four short paragraphs:

1. Name the role and company, and why this opening fits.
2. One proof point from the base resume, tied to a requirement in the job.
3. A second proof point, tied to a different requirement. Skip this paragraph if the resume supports only one.
4. A short close that asks for a conversation. Mention salary, visa, or availability only when the user or the base resume states them.

Address it to a named person when the job description gives one. Otherwise address the hiring team. Sign with the name in the base resume's contact block.

Use "I". Do not paste resume bullets. State the outcome and why it matters for this job.

```markdown
Dear Hiring Team,

I am applying for the Backend Engineer role at Northwind. Your focus on payment reliability matches the billing services I operate.

At Example Co I built event-driven billing on Kafka so payment events survive a service restart. That is the failure mode this role is meant to reduce.

I would welcome a conversation about the role.

Sincerely,
Amir
```

A number, title, or employer that is not in the base resume does not belong in the letter.
